When user types "b", the query is "b". The matching results (strict search?) The search engine is "strict" by default. The listMatchingResults function uses searchEngine. We need to see the search service. Not provided, but we can assume it does a prefix match? The test expects after typing "b", the suggestions are: Banana, Bilberry, Blackberry, Blackcurrant, Blueberry (maxResults=5). Then pressing ArrowDown twice selects the third item (index 2? Actually first ArrowDown selects index 0? Let's see navigation: currentFocus starts at -1. On ArrowDown, currentFocus++ -> 0, then addActive sets aria-selected on list[0]. Second ArrowDown -> currentFocus=1, selects list[1]. So after two ArrowDown, the selected item is index 1 (Bilberry). But the test asserts that after two ArrowDown, aria-selected is true on #autoComplete_result_1. That matches index 1 (Bilberry). Then the user types "l". This triggers a new search with query "bl". The results for "bl": Blackberry, Blackcurrant, Blueberry? Actually "bl" matches Blackberry, Blackcurrant, Blueberry (and maybe Bilberry? "bil" doesn't start with "bl"). So the new results list: Blackberry (index 0), Blackcurrant (index 1), Blueberry (index 2). The test asserts that after typing "l", the text of #autoComplete_result_0 is "Blackberry". Good.

